      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "29a79bcb-9fc9-5872-ae2b-0d4a07413900",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Landscape with Obelisk\n- People: Govert Flinck\n- Organizations: Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum\n- Places: Boston, Massachusetts, United States\n- Events: Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum theft\n- Topics: museum rewards\n\nFacts:\n- In 1638, Govert Flinck painted Landscape with Obelisk.\n- Before 1990, Landscape with Obelisk hung in the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum in Boston, Massachusetts, United States.\n- In the early hours of March 18, 1990, guards at the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum in Boston admitted two men posing as police officers responding to a disturbance call.\n- Landscape with Obelisk was stolen from the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum in 1990.\n- The Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum initially offered a $5 million reward for information leading to the recovery of stolen works.\n- In 2017, the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum temporarily doubled the reward to $10 million until the end of that year.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "afb73067-812e-5dbf-9dba-1a9c4915ff4b",
        "text": "Page: Landscape with Obelisk. Sentence: Landscape with Obelisk is painting by Dutch artist Govert Flinck, painted in 1638.\nPage: Landscape with Obelisk. Sentence: The painting hung in the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum of Boston, Massachusetts, United States, prior to being stolen in 1990.\nPage: Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum theft. Sentence: In the early hours of March 18, 1990, guards at the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum in Boston admitted two men posing as police officers responding to a disturbance call.\nPage: Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum theft. Sentence: The museum initially offered a reward of $5 million for information leading to their recovery, but in 2017 this was doubled temporarily to $10 million with an expiration date set to the end of the year.",
